development.question_text:
Does this graph have line symmetry about the $y$-axis, rotational symmetry about the origin, both, or neither?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[<->,thick,blue] (-1.9,-1.9)--(1.9,1.9);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does this graph have line symmetry about the $y$-axis, rotational symmetry about the origin, both, or neither?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0) circle (1.5);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does this graph have line symmetry about the $y$-axis, rotational symmetry about the origin, both, or neither?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[<->,thick,blue,domain=-2:1.5,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.7*exp(\x*ln(2))});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does this graph have line symmetry about the $y$-axis, rotational symmetry about the origin, both, or neither?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[<->,thick,blue,domain=-1.35:1.35,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.8*\x*\x*\x});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does this graph have line symmetry about the $y$-axis, rotational symmetry about the origin, both, or neither?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[<->,thick,blue] (-1.9,1.1)--(1.9,1.1);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which line is the axis of symmetry of the triangle below?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[thick] (0,1.7)--(-1.2,-0.9)--(1.2,-0.9)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

State the number of lines of symmetry and the order of rotational symmetry of this shape.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (22.5:1.6)--(67.5:1.6)--(112.5:1.6)--(157.5:1.6)--(202.5:1.6)--(247.5:1.6)--(292.5:1.6)--(337.5:1.6)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

State the number of lines of symmetry and the order of rotational symmetry of this shape.
